  "text": "The drawbacks next: sweetened bottles can change the whole deal. Added sugar can turn a useful fermented drink into something much closer to a liquid dessert. Milk allergy is still a hard stop. Fermentation can change the lactose, but it does not remove the milk proteins that trigger an allergy. The sour, slightly funky flavour is not for everyone. Plain kefir tastes much tangier than ordinary milk or sweetened yogurt.",
